 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  J|p=3/2+ for {+33}S ground state (2025Ch07).                           
 34S  c  1987Wa20: {+33}S(n,|a) with E{-n}=0.010-1 MeV at the Geel Electron     
 34S 2c  Linear Accelerator (GELINA). |a particles were detected using a large  
 34S 3c  surface barrier detector. Measured integrated (n,|a) cross sections.   
 34S 4c  Deduced resonance parameters.                                          
 34S  c  1987Co23: {+33}S(n,n) with E=0.010-2 MeV at the Oak Ridge Electron     
 34S 2c  Linear Accelerator (ORELA). Neutrons were detected using a NE-110      
 34S 3c  scintillator. Measured total {+33}S(n,n) cross sections. Deduced       
 34S 4c  resonance parameters.                                                  
 34S  c  1975Au06: {+33}S(n,|a{-0}) with E{-n}=10-700 keV at the Los Alamos     
 34S 2c  Scientific Laboratory (LASL) vertical Van de Graaff accelerator. |a    
 34S 3c  particles were detected using silicon surface barrier detectors.       
 34S 4c  Measured {+33}S(n,|a{-0}) cross sections. {+33}S(n,|g) with            
 34S 5c  E{-n}=2.5-850 keV at the Oak Ridge Electron Linear Accelerator (ORELA).
 34S 6c  |g rays were detected using two NE-226 fluorocarbon liquid             
 34S 7c  scintillators. Measured {+33}S(n,|g) cross sections. Deduced resonance 
 34S 8c  parameters.                                                            
 34S  c  2018MuZY: Atlas of Neutron Resonances. Evaluation of neutron resonance 
 34S 2c  energies, spins, width parameters, and resonance strengths for nuclei  
 34S 3c  of Z=1-60.                                                             
